**How to implement.** The online-source seam in Domain: its record, its in-memory double and its facts (001 §D '`MaterialSourceProxy` (search, fetch) with adapters'; 001 §P '`MaterialSourceProxy` (online sources)', 'every proxy has an in-memory stub of the same shape'; the S13.1 brief: search, fetch and update the snapshot, per adapter; .spec-md §5 `MaterialSourceProxy`; §10.2: per-file progress with Cancel). One proxy is one adapter: this section's refractiveindex.info (step 447) and S13.2's PTB and Henke sources are each a `MaterialSourceProxy`. The proxy does IO only; what a pull writes is step 444's. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialSources.fs`, `module MaterialSources` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly before `CatalogueImport.fs` (step 37), because the import context carries the sources (step 444): one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. It opens `MaterialLibrary`, `LibraryEntryFiles` and `System.Threading`. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. In order: (1) `MaterialSourceError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `SourceSnapshotMissingErr` (the source holds no snapshot yet), `SourceRecordMissingErr` (the snapshot does not list the record), `SourceRecordUnreadableErr` (the record's page does not parse), `SourceSnapshotIoErr` (the snapshot folder could not be read or written), `SourceDownloadErr` (the source's archive could not be downloaded), `SourceArchiveInvalidErr` (the downloaded archive is not the source's database) and `UnsupportedSnapshotSchemaErr` (a snapshot stamp of another schema version), with `member this.describe : string` rendering each in step 39's form: `the source holds no snapshot: <reason>`, `the snapshot does not list the record: <reason>`, `the record could not be read: <reason>`, `the snapshot could not be read or written: <reason>`, `the source's archive could not be downloaded: <reason>`, `the archive is not the source's database: <reason>` and `the snapshot stamp has another schema version: <reason>`. (2) `MaterialSourceHit = { record : MaterialSourceRecordId; name : EntryName }` (step 24's `MaterialSourceRecordId`): one record a search finds and the name a pulled material takes. (3) `MaterialSourceQuery of string` with `.value` and `member this.filter (hits : MaterialSourceHit list) : MaterialSourceHit list`, the one search rule every adapter applies: the query's text is split on white space into words; a hit is kept when each word occurs, ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`), in its name's text or in its record's text; an empty or blank query keeps every hit; kept hits keep their order. (4) `SourceMaterialRecord = { pull : SourcePullInfo; material : MaterialEntry }`: a fetched record, its pull provenance (step 24, with step 441's `recordHash`) and the material its page parses into, named by its hit, under an id the pull replaces (step 444). (5) `SourceSnapshotFileCount of int` with `.value`; `SourceSnapshotProgress = { filesDone : SourceSnapshotFileCount; filesTotal : SourceSnapshotFileCount }`, told after each file a snapshot update writes; `[<ReferenceEquality>] SourceSnapshotObserver = { reportSnapshotProgress : SourceSnapshotProgress -> unit; cancellation : CancellationToken }`, asked before each file whether the update is cancelled, the rule of `JobRunner.fs:runLoop` and of `KitArchiveObserver` (step 197), with `static member unobserved : SourceSnapshotObserver` telling nobody and never cancelled (`CancellationToken.None`); `SourceSnapshotInfo = { version : MaterialSourceVersion; files : SourceSnapshotFileCount }`; and `SourceSnapshotOutcome` = `SourceSnapshotUpdated of SourceSnapshotInfo` | `SourceSnapshotCancelled` (the update stopped before its next file and left the held snapshot as it was). (6) `[<ReferenceEquality>] MaterialSourceProxy = { sourceName : MaterialSourceName; snapshotVersion : unit -> Result<MaterialSourceVersion option, MaterialSourceError>; searchRecords : MaterialSourceQuery -> Result<MaterialSourceHit list, MaterialSourceError>; fetchRecord : MaterialSourceRecordId -> Result<SourceMaterialRecord, MaterialSourceError>; updateSnapshot : SourceSnapshotObserver -> Result<SourceSnapshotOutcome, MaterialSourceError> }`, the functional-proxy convention (AGENTS.md), each field with a one-line doc: `sourceName` is the source the adapter reads (data, not IO); `snapshotVersion` the held snapshot's version, `None` before the first update; `searchRecords` the held snapshot's catalog through the query's `filter`, `SourceSnapshotMissingErr` without a snapshot; `fetchRecord` one listed record, parsed, under the held snapshot's version, `SourceSnapshotMissingErr` without a snapshot and `SourceRecordMissingErr` for a record its catalog does not list; `updateSnapshot` replaces the held snapshot by the source's current one, reporting and reading the cancellation per file, and a cancelled or failed update keeps the held snapshot. (7) The double. `InMemorySourceRecord = { hit : MaterialSourceHit; recordHash : ContentHash; citation : EntryCitation; material : MaterialEntry }` is one record as a test publishes it. `InMemoryMaterialSource` is a sealed class whose state (the held snapshot's version and records, and the published ones the next update installs) is private and mutated only inside its members and the proxy's closures, as `InMemoryArchiveDisk` keeps its own (step 197): `static member create (name : MaterialSourceName) (licence : EntryLicence) : InMemoryMaterialSource` holds no snapshot and publishes none; `member this.publish (version : MaterialSourceVersion) (records : InMemorySourceRecord list) : unit` sets what the next update installs. `type MaterialSourceProxy with static member createInMemory (source : InMemoryMaterialSource) : MaterialSourceProxy` answers the five fields of (6) over it: `searchRecords` filters the held records' hits; `fetchRecord` answers `{ pull = { source; record; recordHash; sourceVersion = <the held version>; licence; citation }; material = { <the record's material> with name = <its hit's name> } }`; `updateSnapshot` with nothing published is `SourceDownloadErr` naming the source, and otherwise, before each published record, reads the cancellation (cancelled, it answers `SourceSnapshotCancelled` with the held snapshot unchanged) and after each reports progress; once every record is counted the published snapshot becomes the held one, and the answer is `SourceSnapshotUpdated` of its version and record count. No caching, retry, option or other field is added (.spec-md §8). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourceProxyTests.fs`, `module MaterialSourceProxyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its double is `InMemoryMaterialSource.create (MaterialSourceName "Test source") (EntryLicence "CC0-1.0")`; its records are the catalogue's Silicon and Langasite (`BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`, decoded through `toMaterialEntry`), published as `Si (Silicon), Aspnes` at `main/Si/nk/Aspnes.yml` and `La3Ga5SiO14 (Langasite), Test` at `other/La3Ga5SiO14/nk/Test.yml`, with test-local hashes and citations. `a source holds no snapshot until its first update`: `snapshotVersion` answers `Ok None`, and `searchRecords` and `fetchRecord` answer `SourceSnapshotMissingErr`. `an update installs the published snapshot, reporting each record once`: after `publish` of version `2026-11-01`, `updateSnapshot` under an observer recording each progress answers `SourceSnapshotUpdated { version = MaterialSourceVersion "2026-11-01"; files = SourceSnapshotFileCount 2 }`, the progress reading 1 and 2 of 2, and `snapshotVersion` answers that version. `a search keeps the hits whose name or record holds every word, ignoring case`: `silicon`, `SI ASPNES` and `nk` keep, in catalog order, the hits that hold them; `aspnes langasite` keeps none; and a blank query keeps both. `a fetched record carries its pull provenance and its material under its hit's name`: `fetchRecord` of the Silicon record answers its `SourcePullInfo` (the source, the record, its hash, the held version, the licence and its citation) and Silicon's material named `Si (Silicon), Aspnes`; an unlisted record answers `SourceRecordMissingErr`. `an update cancelled before its next record keeps the held snapshot`: with `2026-11-01` held and `2026-11-04` published, a token whose source is cancelled on the first progress makes `updateSnapshot` answer `SourceSnapshotCancelled`, and `snapshotVersion` still answers `2026-11-01`. `an update with nothing published is SourceDownloadErr`: a fresh double's `updateSnapshot` answers `SourceDownloadErr`. `every material-source error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it.

**Acceptance.** After the seam lands, `MaterialSources.fs` MUST declare `MaterialSourceProxy` with exactly `sourceName`, `snapshotVersion`, `searchRecords`, `fetchRecord` and `updateSnapshot`, its in-memory double `MaterialSourceProxy.createInMemory` and the one search rule `MaterialSourceQuery.filter`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a source holds no snapshot until its first update`, `an update installs the published snapshot, reporting each record once`, `a search keeps the hits whose name or record holds every word, ignoring case`, `a fetched record carries its pull provenance and its material under its hit's name`, `an update cancelled before its next record keeps the held snapshot`, `an update with nothing published is SourceDownloadErr` and `every material-source error renders its condition and its payload` under `MaterialSourceProxyTests`, the count rising by 7; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
